 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-10-25 (10): passive mobs spawn more often, counted around the player (**NOT b1.7.3**; `world/mobs.rs` was compiled and its 20 tests run in a Linux scratch crate (rustc 1.75, the `world` modules without `lib.rs`); the rest of mc-rs is not compiled; +1 test `mobs::tests::animals_refill_fast_never_crowd_and_keep_apart`; run `cargo test --lib mobs` first). Was: one pack (1..4 of a kind) every 400 ticks (20 s) at a point 24..48 blocks off, and only while the whole list held fewer than 12 animals, so a killed herd took 20 s and more to come back and a stray 100 blocks away held the refill.
+    - `Mobs::spawn`: an attempt every `ANIMAL_EVERY` = 100 ticks (squid stay at 400); animals are counted within `NEAR` = 48 blocks of the player (`Mobs::count_near`, also used by `pack` for animals; monsters and squid keep their global counts, `ANYWHERE`), `CAP_ANIMALS` stays 12 so the ceiling around you is the old one; an attempt happens with chance (12 - near) / 12, so the herds ease into the cap and slow down as the surroundings fill; the point must have no animal within `SPACING` = 12 blocks (herds spread out; a pack is still 1..4 within 5 blocks) and no pack starts of a kind that already has `CAP_KIND` = 5 around (a mix of kinds). The burst at start is unchanged.
+    - Test (flat grass, the player standing, 6 seeds, 3000 ticks): 6 to 10 animals around after 400 ticks (the old rule: at most 4), never more than 13 around, at most 7 of a kind, the middle of a new pack at least 11.8 blocks from the nearest animal.
+    - ponytail: nothing is spawned out of sight (as before they appear 24+ blocks away, in front of you too), animals beyond 32 blocks still despawn 1 in 800 a tick after 600 (a faster refill churns a little more), no biome weights. UNVERIFIED: every number by eye (5 s, 12 blocks, 5 a kind) and how it feels on a device.
 - 2026-10-25 (9): a bed tapped by day says "You can only sleep at night" (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; no test, `use_bed` needs the whole `App`). `EntityPlayer.sleepInBedAt` answers NOT_POSSIBLE_NOW by day and `BlockBed.blockActivated` shows `tile.bed.noSleep`; `use_bed` returned silently. The one-line message of the pack (`hint`, 2.5 s, lower middle) now carries its text in `hint_msg`, so the bed reuses it (a live, awake player only, as vanilla's order of checks).
     - ponytail: no other status message (too far, monsters near). UNVERIFIED: the wording (the lang file, from memory), that it compiles (two fields set by one tuple assignment, `hint_msg` read in the HUD pass beside `v`).
 - 2026-10-25 (8): organic mob movement from `EntityLiving` (b1.7.3 decompiled), every mob, closer to b1.7.3 and not away from it; written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +3 tests `mobs::tests::{a_mob_eases_into_a_walk_and_glides_to_a_stop, the_body_trails_the_head_and_follows_the_walk, a_mob_looking_at_the_player_tips_its_head_toward_their_eyes}`; run `cargo test --lib mobs items` first. What was stiff: the walk speed was set outright every frame (a mob started and stopped at full speed and a hop lost its run), the body pointed where `yaw` pointed, and `yaw` moves in 20 Hz steps (up to 30 degrees at once), so every turn was a jerk.
